  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/indices.html#events-2:window-14\r\n\r\n> the document has finished loading\r\n\r\nIs there any specification of what exactly constitutes \"finished loading\"? I understand what that implies, but is there a strict definition by WHATWG in this or other specifications, or are user agents free to interpret \"loading finished\" as they please?\r\n\r\n[7.8.2](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#read-html) doesn't help much -- it says:\r\n\r\n> When no more bytes are available, the user agent must queue a task on the networking task source for the parser to process the implied EOF character, which eventually causes a load event to be fired.\r\n\r\nI thought that'd be \"DOMContentLoaded\" event, when document is parsed, I mean?",
